# Intent & Data Correctness Verification

**Passing a click, HTTP 200, or unit test is not enough.** Before handoff, prove the change does what the **user expects the data to become**, not merely that the control responded.

Complements **`rigorous-qa-before-handoff.mdc`**, **`verify-ui-before-done.mdc`**, **`bug-check-before-return.mdc`**, and **`definition_of_done.mdc`**.

## The failure mode to avoid

| What agents often check | What users actually care about |
| --- | --- |
| Button click fires | **Only** the intended rows/items remain |
| Page loads | **Every visible field** is correct on real data |
| API returns 200 | **Response body** matches what the UI will show |
| Service/tinker returns field X | **HTTP JSON** on the SPA route includes X (see **`api-resource-enrichment-wiring.mdc`**) |
| "Looks wired up" | **Sibling controls** behave the same way |

## Step 1 — Write an Intent Contract (before saying done)

For **each** new or changed behavior (filter, button, form, job, export, API field), write one line:

> **When** [user action] **→ expect** [observable outcome on real data]

Examples:

- When user clicks **Rejected** → list shows **only** rejected orders; row count = pill count.
- When user saves deposit → **Balance** column and API `balance` field both update on that row.
- When sync job finishes → reported counts match DB rows; no skipped SKUs the user will miss.

If you cannot state the expected outcome in one line, you do not understand the requirement yet — clarify or infer from siblings/spec before handoff.

## Step 2 — Act → Observe → Compare (mandatory)

After performing the user action on the **real path** (browser, API, job, export file):

1. **Observe** — record counts, sample row IDs/SKUs, field values, URL/query, toasts, file contents.
2. **Compare** — every observation must match the Intent Contract.
3. **Purity check** — scan **all** visible results (not just the first row). Any item that violates the contract = **fail**.
4. **Count check** — when the UI shows a number (pill, badge, total, pagination), the list length or aggregate must match.
5. **Cross-layer** — when UI reads an API/DB field, spot-check that layer too for at least one sample row.
6. **Sibling consistency** — controls that look or sit together (tabs, group pills, column filters) must follow the **same selection semantics** unless spec says otherwise.

## Applies to (not only filters)

| Surface | Compare against |
| --- | --- |
| List/table filters & sorts | Visible rows + counts + key column values |
| Forms & inline edit | Saved value in UI reload + API/DB |
| Dialogs & bulk actions | Affected row count + persisted state |
| Reports & exports | Column semantics, totals, row count |
| API endpoints | Typed contract + realistic seeded/live payload |
| Jobs & sync | Log counters vs actual rows; no silent partial failure |

## Stop conditions (not done)

- Visible rows include items that should be excluded.
- Displayed count ≠ actual count.
- Field shows null/wrong value on a row the user will see.
- Behavior differs from a sibling control without an documented reason.
- Only the happy path was checked; no clear, deselect, error, or empty state.

## Forbidden handoffs

- "Clicked it and the page updated" without outcome evidence.
- "Tests pass" when Intent Contract was not checked on real data.
- "Should work" / "try hard refresh" instead of fixing or listing gaps.

If blocked (auth, no data, service down), say **incomplete** and what was not verified.

## Agent vs user

| Agent (mandatory, internal) | User reply (default) |
| --- | --- |
| Full Intent Contract + Act → Observe → Compare | Brief **Verified** note with outcomes |
| Purity, counts, cross-layer, siblings | No wall of tables unless asked or failed |
| Fix until pass or disclose blocked | Clear gaps only when something could not run |

The user should not need to re-test to discover wrong data — that is the agent’s job, not the agent’s homework to paste into chat.
